        "descriptions": [
          {
            "description": "Source code and namelists of the Geoscientific Model Development technical paper: Multiple same-level and telescoping nesting in GFDL's dynamical core.<br> This paper studies the landfall of hurricane Laura (2020) and an Atmospheric river hitting California (2021) using global and regional domains with multiple same level and telescoping nested grids.<br> <br> The official source code to compile SHiELD is taken from:<br> 1- FV3: tag: FV3-202107-public<br> https://github.com/NOAA-GFDL/GFDL_atmos_cubed_sphere<br> 2- FMS: tag: 2021.02<br> https://github.com/NOAA-GFDL/GFDL_atmos_cubed_sphere<br> 3- SHiELD_physics: tag: SHiELD_v2021b (with a minor code change)<br> https://github.com/NOAA-GFDL/SHiELD_physics The input namelists are for the cases shown in this study:<br> 1- Global C48 + nests<br> 2- Global C768 + nests<br> 3- Regional R192 + nests The nests parameters, used in each of the top parent grid cases C48, C768 and R192, are set similarly (except for the nest dimensions and time steps which could be found in the original paper) but differ from case to case.",
            "descriptionType": "Abstract"
          }
